  "question": {
    "text": "Consider an obtuse angled triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> in which the difference between the largest and the smallest angle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> and whose sides are in arithmetic progression. Suppose that the vertices of this triangle lie on a circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>.<br />\n(There are two questions based on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PARAGRAPH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#34;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#34;</mo></math>, the question given below is one of them)<br>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> be the area of the triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>. Then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>64</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1008",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;be obtuse angle and let sides be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></math></p><p>So, plotting the diagram we get,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0001_f45290f7120f.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 155px;\" /></p><p>Now let sides be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></math></p><p>Also given angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>And circum radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Now by sine rule we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>C</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>C</mi></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Now using cosine rule we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8722;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8722;</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>B</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>From <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math><br />Area of triangle<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Now&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>64</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>36</mn><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>252</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1008</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}